{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__General_Awareness__Static_GK__Culture__Festivals__SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_223","path":"organized/Others/General Awareness/Static GK/Culture & Festivals/@SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC SUPER PRACTICE_223.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/General Awareness/Static GK/Culture & Festivals","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following belongs to Patiala Gharana?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2346;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Ali Baksh Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Nathu Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2366;&#2341;&#2370; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Abdul Wahid Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2342; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Chhaju Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2331;&#2332;&#2381;&#2332;&#2370; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The Patiala Gharana of Hindustani classical music was founded in the mid-19th century by Ustad <b>Ali Baksh Khan</b> and his friend Ustad Fateh Ali Khan (who were known as \"Aliya-Fattu\"). Ali Baksh Khan was the father of the legendary Ustad Bade Ghulam Ali Khan, who is one of the most celebrated exponents of this gharana.</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options:</b></p><p>&#8226; Nathu Khan: A sarangi player, possibly associated with various styles but not a founder of Patiala Gharana in the primary sense.</p><p>&#8226; Abdul Wahid Khan: One of the founders of the Kirana Gharana.</p><p>&#8226; Chhaju Khan: Associated with the Bhendibazaar Gharana.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#8226; The Patiala Gharana is known for its romantic and expressive style, intricate taans (fast melodic passages), layakari (rhythmic play), and the use of sargams (solfege).</p><p>&#8226; It incorporates elements from other gharanas like Gwalior, Jaipur, and Kirana.</p><p>&#8226; Prominent vocalists of this gharana include Ustad Bade Ghulam Ali Khan, Ustad Amanat Ali Khan, Ustad Fateh Ali Khan (nephew of Bade Ghulam Ali Khan), Parveen Sultana, and Ajoy Chakrabarty.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following established the Indore gharana?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2311;&#2306;&#2342;&#2380;&#2352; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Bhimsen Joshi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2368;&#2350;&#2360;&#2375;&#2344; &#2332;&#2379;&#2358;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ustad Amir Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Tansen</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2360;&#2375;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ustad Ghaghe Khuda Baksh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2328;&#2366;&#2328;&#2375; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2366; &#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><b>Ustad Amir Khan</b>, a legendary Hindustani classical vocalist, founded the Indore gharana, known for its slow-tempo (vilambit) khayal singing and deep, introspective style. </p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options</b>: </p><p>&#183; <b>Bhimsen Joshi</b>: Incorrect, as he was associated with the Kirana gharana.</p><p>&#183; <b>Tansen</b>: Incorrect, as Tansen, a 16th-century musician, predates the Indore gharana.</p><p>&#183; <b>Ustad Ghaghe Khuda Baksh</b>: Incorrect, as he is not credited with founding the Indore gharana.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>______ is often touted as the Tansen of the 20th century, blending classical music with a unique style.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">______ &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352; 20&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2360;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2360;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2361;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2370;&#2336;&#2368; &#2358;&#2376;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404;</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Ustad Ali Baksh Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Bade Ghulam Ali Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2350; &#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mubarak Ali Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2369;&#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325; &#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Barkat Ali Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2352;&#2325;&#2340; &#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Bade Ghulam Ali Khan, from the Patiala Gharana, was a legendary Indian classical vocalist known for his unique style.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Match the following musical instruments with the maestros who played them. </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Instrument</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Maestro</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">a. Santoor</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. Bismillah Khan</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">b. Sitar</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. Ustad Binda Khan</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">c. Shehnai</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. Pt. Shiv Kumar Sharma</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">d. Sarangi</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. Anushka Shankar</td></tr></table></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">a. &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2370;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. &#2348;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2361; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">b. &#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2366; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">c. &#2358;&#2361;&#2344;&#2366;&#2312;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. &#2346;&#2306;. &#2358;&#2367;&#2357; &#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">d. &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2359;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352;</td></tr></table></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;-iv, &#2348;&#2368;-iii, &#2360;&#2368;-ii, &#2337;&#2368;-i</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;-&#2310;&#2312;, &#2348;&#2368;-II, &#2360;&#2368;-III, &#2337;&#2368;-IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;-ii, &#2348;&#2368;-iii, &#2360;&#2368;-i, &#2337;&#2368;-iv</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;-iii, &#2348;&#2368;-iv, &#2360;&#2368;-i, &#2337;&#2368;-ii</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>&#61623; Santoor - Pt. Shiv Kumar Sharma</p><p>&#183; Pt. Shiv Kumar Sharma is the most famous Santoor player in India and is credited with popularizing it in Hindustani classical music.</p><p>&#61623; Sitar - Anoushka Shankar</p><p>&#183; Anoushka Shankar, daughter of Ravi Shankar, is an internationally recognized Sitar player.</p><p>&#61623; Shehnai - Ustad Bismillah Khan</p><p>&#183; Ustad Bismillah Khan is synonymous with the Shehnai and played a crucial role in elevating its status in classical music.</p><p>&#61623; Sarangi - Ustad Binda Khan</p><p>&#183; Ustad Binda Khan was a noted Sarangi player in Hindustani classical music.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Famous musician Shakoor Khan was associated with which of the following musical instruments?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2325;&#2370;&#2352; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351; &#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Sitar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarod</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2379;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarangi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Santoor</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2370;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><b>Ustad Shakoor Khan (1905-1975) was one of the outstanding sarangi players</b> of the twentieth century. He was firmly identified with the Kirana Gharana, being the nephew and student of Ustad Abdul Waheed Khan.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is called the cyclic arrangement of time units in Hindustani Classical music?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2361;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Alap</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2354;&#2366;&#2346;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Raga</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2366;&#2327;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Tala</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Jati</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2367;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>&#183; <b>Tala</b> refers to the <b>cyclic rhythmic framework</b> in Hindustani classical music. </p><p>&#183; Each Tala has a specific number of beats (matras) arranged in groups called vibhags, and these cycles repeat throughout the performance. </p><p>&#183; Musicians keep track of the Tala through hand gestures called kriyas (including claps and waves), which mark important points in the rhythmic cycle.</p><p>&#183; Examples: <i>Teental</i> (16 beats), <i>Jhaptal</i> (10 beats), <i>Ektaal</i> (12 beats).</p><p>Why Not Others?</p><p>&#183; <b>Alap</b>: Unmetered, free-flowing melodic introduction.</p><p>&#183; <b>Raga</b>: Melodic scale/mood (not time-bound).</p><p>&#183; <b>Jati </b>: Classification of ragas or talas by structure.</p><p><b>Key Point</b>: Tala is the <b>metrical cycle</b> that musicians and percussionists (e.g., tabla players) follow.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>With which of the following musical instruments is the musician Zakir Hussain associated?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367;&#2352; &#2361;&#2369;&#2360;&#2376;&#2344; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351; &#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Dhol</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2338;&#2379;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Vichitra Veena</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Tanpura</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Tabla</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2348;&#2354;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><b>Ustad Zakir Hussain</b> (born 9 March 1951) is an Indian tabla player, composer, percussionist, music producer and film actor.</p><p>He was awarded the Padma shari in 1988, the Padma Bhushan in 2002, and the Padma Vibhushan in 2023, by the Government of India.<sup> </sup>He was also awarded the Govt of India's Sangeet Natak Academy in 1990, Fellowship of the Sangeet Natak Academy fellowship Ratna Sadsya in 2018.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Where is the renowned Bhatkhande Music Institute located?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2349;&#2366;&#2340;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2361;&#2366;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Lucknow</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2326;&#2344;&#2314;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Chennai</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Surat</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2352;&#2340;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Madurai</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2342;&#2369;&#2352;&#2376;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>&#183; The renowned <b>Bhatkhande Music Institute</b> is located in <b>Lucknow</b>, Uttar Pradesh. </p><p>&#183; Bhatkhande Music Institute University, formerly known as \"Marris College of Hindustani Music\" was established by Pt. Vishnu Narayan Bhatkhande in July 1926. </p><p>&#183; The purpose of its establishment was to liberate music from the monopoly of Gharanedar Musicians and make music education accessible to all.</p><p>&#183; The Marris College was established due to the untiring efforts of devoted and dedicated connoisseurs of Art and Musicians like Late Pt. Vishnu Narayan Bhatkhande, Late Rai Umanath Bali, Late Raja Nawab Ali Khan and many others.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ishwari Prasad is credited to have introduced the ________ Gharana of Kathak.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2312;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2341;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; ________ &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2351; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Jaipur</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2351;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Raigarh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2327;&#2338;&#2364;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Lucknow</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2326;&#2344;&#2314;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Banaras</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Lucknow Gharana is one of the main gharanas out of the three in Kathak, the other two being Jaipur and Banaras. It represents the lasting Mughal influence on Kathak and was introduced to Lucknow by Maharaj Iswari Prasad Misra and his brothers and further evolved into a court dance over the years. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Annapurna Devi, who was awarded the Padma Bhushan, was a famous player of which of the following instruments?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2342;&#2381;&#2350; &#2349;&#2370;&#2359;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2325; &#2341;&#2368;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Sarod</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2379;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Santoor</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2370;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Veena</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Surbahar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2348;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Padma Bhushan recipient Annapurna Devi, a legendary musician, was renowned for her mastery of the <b>Surbahar</b> musical instrument.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The Guinness world record for the highest number of songs recorded in a day is held by an Indian Playback Singer. How many songs in a day were recorded?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2368;&#2332; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2348;&#2376;&#2325; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2341;&#2375;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">34</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The Indian playback singer Kumar Sanu is the world record holder for recording <b>28 songs</b> in a single day. And that record has not been broken by anyone yet.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>KishoriAmonkar is famous for which of the following forms of music?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2350;&#2379;&#2344;&#2325;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Bhajan singing</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2332;&#2344; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ghazal singing</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2332;&#2364;&#2354; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Hindustani classical vocals</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Carnatic classical vocals</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><b>KishoriAmonkar</b> (10 April 1932  -  3 April 2017) was a <b>leading Indian classical vocalist</b>, belonging to the Jaipur gharana, or a community of musicians sharing a distinctive musical style. She was a performer of the classical genre khyal and the light classical genres thumri and bhajan.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>_____ was first trained in classical music under her father Ustad 'Baba' Allauddin Khan, and established the Maihar-Senia gharana with his help.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>_____ &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; '&#2348;&#2366;&#2348;&#2366;' &#2309;&#2354;&#2366;&#2313;&#2342;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368;&#2344; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2361;&#2340; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2342;&#2342; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2361;&#2352;-&#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Anupama Bhagwat</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2350;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2357;&#2340;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Annapurna Devi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Roopa Panesar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2370;&#2346;&#2366; &#2346;&#2344;&#2375;&#2360;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sahana Banerjee</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2344;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><b>Annapurna Devi was first trained in classical music </b>under her father Ustad 'Baba' Allauddin Khan, and established the Maihar-Senia gharana with his help. Annapurna Devi, a prominent figure of Hindustani classical music, born in Maihar, Madhya Pradesh in 1927.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Shattantri Veena, meaning a Veena with hundred strings, is the ancient Sanskrit name of which instrument?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2340;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376; &#2360;&#2380; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;, &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351; &#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2330;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2344;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Tambura/Tanpura</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366;/&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarangi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarod</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2379;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Santoor</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2370;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>&bull; Shattantri Veena is the ancient Sanskrit name of the Santoor.</p><p>&bull; Shivkumar Sharma was a renowned Indian classical musician and santoor player credited with adapting the santoor for Indian classical music. </p><p>&bull; He received the Padma Shri in 1991 and the Padma Vibhushan in 200(1)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ustad Asad Ali Khan was one of the masters of the ___________.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2360;&#2342; &#2309;&#2354;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344; ___________ &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">sarangi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">mridangam</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2371;&#2342;&#2306;&#2327;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">tanpura</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">rudra veena</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Ustad Asad Ali Khan (1937 - 2011) was a highly acclaimed Indian musician and one of the foremost exponents of the rudra veena, an ancient plucked string instrument used in Hindustani classical music. He belonged to the Khandarbani dhrupad tradition.</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options:</b></p><p>&#183; Sarangi: The sarangi is a bowed short-necked string instrument from the Indian subcontinent used in Hindustani classical music.</p><p>&#183; Mridangam: The mridangam is a double-sided drum, a primary rhythmic accompaniment in Carnatic music.</p><p>&#183; Tanpura: The tanpura (or tambura) is a long-necked plucked string instrument used to provide a continuous harmonic drone in Indian classical music. </p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#183; The rudra veena is a large plucked string instrument with a deep, resonant sound, considered one of the oldest and most revered instruments in Indian classical music.</p><p>&#183; Ustad Asad Ali Khan was a recipient of several prestigious awards, including the Padma Bhushan (2008) and the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1977), for his contributions to Indian classical music.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Pandit Ananda Gopal Bandopadhyay was a ________ player of the Banaras gharana.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2344;&#2306;&#2342; &#2327;&#2379;&#2346;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342;&#2379;&#2346;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2351; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2360; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; ________ &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2325; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Sarangi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarod</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2379;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sitar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Tabla</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2348;&#2354;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>&bull; <b>Ananda Gopal Bandopadhyay</b> (April 28, 1942  -  May 7, 2021) was an Indian tabla player. He was trained in the style of the Benaras Gharana by his teacher Mahadev Prasad Mishra.</p><p>&bull; His father, Radha Gopal Bandopadhyay, was an amateur vocalist.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The famous musician Satyadev Pawar is associated with which musical instrument?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2342;&#2375;&#2357; &#2346;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Violin</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2379;&#2354;&#2367;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Shehnai</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2361;&#2344;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Veena</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2368;&#2339;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sitar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Satyadev Pawar, the renowned musician, is associated with the <b>violin</b>. He initiated his musical journey at the age of eleven in the former Jodhpur State of Rajasthan, India. His expertise and contributions have significantly enriched the realm of Indian classical music.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Gangubai Hangal was an Indian vocalist of Hindustani classical tradition who was awarded the Sangeet Natak Academy Award in 1973. From which of the following musical Gharanas did she belong?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2327;&#2306;&#2327;&#2370;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2306;&#2327;&#2354; &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352;&#2306;&#2346;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 1973 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325; &#2309;&#2325;&#2366;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2341;&#2368;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Banaras Gharana</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2360; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Patiala Gharana</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Kirana Gharana</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Agra Gharana</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2327;&#2352;&#2366; &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>An exponent of Hindustani classical music, GangubaiHangal was an eminent singer to have hailed from the <b>Kirana gharana</b> of the Hindustani khyal family.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Bhajan Sopori, a Padma Shri awardee, is a _________ player.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2342;&#2381;&#2350; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2332;&#2344; &#2360;&#2379;&#2346;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; _________ &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">sitar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">santoor</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2370;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">tabla</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2348;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">violin</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2354;&#2367;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Pandit Bhajan Sopori (1948 - 2022) was a legendary Indian musician and a maestro of the <b>santoor</b>, a stringed musical instrument native to Kashmir. He was a recipient of the Padma Shri, India's fourth-highest civilian award, in 2004.</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options:</b></p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Sitar: A plucked stringed instrument used in Hindustani classical music.</p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Tabla: A pair of twin hand drums, the principal percussion instrument in Hindustani classical music.</p><p><b>&#8226; </b>Violin: A bowed string instrument, used in both Western classical music and adapted for Indian classical music.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#8226; Bhajan Sopori belonged to the Sufiana gharana of Kashmir and played a significant role in popularizing the santoor on the national and international stage.</p><p>&#8226; He was known for his innovative playing style and his efforts to preserve the traditional music of Kashmir.</p><p>&#8226; He was also a composer and musicologist and established the SaMaPa (Sopori Academy of Music and Performing Arts) to promote Indian classical music.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ustad Hassu Khan, Ustad Haddu Khan and Ustad Nathu Khan were exponents of the ___________ Gharana.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2361;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2370; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2361;&#2342;&#2381;&#2342;&#2370; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2342; &#2344;&#2366;&#2341;&#2370; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344; ___________ &#2328;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2325; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Benaras</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Gwalior</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Delhi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Patiala</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><b>The Gwalior Gharana </b>evolved during the time of the Mughal Empire (1526 CE  -  1857 CE). Among the early masters (ustad) were Naththan Khan, Naththan Pir Bakhsh and his grandsons Haddu, Hassu and Natthu Khan. The head musician in the imperial court was Bade Mohammad Khan, who was famous for his taanbazi style.</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}